        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "6d3863df-3461-53c5-8232-090ac2592e49",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Irish National Caucus, Ancient Order of Hibernians, American Irish Political Education Committee, Amnesty International\n- People: Father Sean Gabriel Mc Manus, Seán McManus, John Finucane, Seán MacBride, Inez McCormack\n- Concepts: MacBride Principles, Good Friday Agreement\n\nFacts:\n- The Ancient Order of Hibernians was founded in New York City in 1836.\n- The Irish National Caucus was founded by Father Sean Gabriel Mc Manus on February 6, 1974, at a meeting of the Ancient Order of Hibernians.\n- The MacBride Principles were launched in November 1984.\n- Seán McManus and the Irish National Caucus promoted the MacBride Principles.\n- John Finucane and the American Irish Political Education Committee promoted the MacBride Principles.\n- Nobel Laureate Seán MacBride, a founding member of Amnesty International, drafted the MacBride Principles.\n- The Ancient Order of Hibernians now has its largest membership in the United States.\n- Inez McCormack was a signatory to the MacBride Principles for fair employment.\n- Inez McCormack successfully campaigned for the inclusion of strong equality and human rights provisions in the Good Friday Agreement.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "d71d7956-ab52-5e85-b723-6d3e88c3b8a4",
